# Archived legacy workspaces (folded in 2026-08-13, not version-controlled)
/_archive/

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS temporary
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Python (in case we add validation scripts)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Session ephemera (not RB-canonical)
# (Add patterns here as the workflow surfaces them.)
# Scratch build output from ad-hoc deck/workbook generation (contains node_modules,
# rendered previews, intermediate build dirs) — regeneratable, not RB system state.
# RB-2026-09-05: /output/ (singular) removed -- confirmed zero live script
# references, only a single stale leftover file (archived). /outputs/ is the
# one real scratch dir; kept as the only pattern here going forward.
/outputs/
/tmp/

# Computed caches — derived from canonical files, regeneratable.
system/.cache/

# Team Portal raw request-traffic log — high-volume, no editorial value
# in git history (unlike system/audit/'s curated low-volume events).
system/team/usage_log/

# RB API request log — high-volume and can contain live credentials
# (e.g. x_api_key query params) logged verbatim from real requests.
system/api/request.log

# Automation runtime logs.
system/automation/*.log
system/automation/*.error.log

# Generated daily brief artifacts — built by morning_pipeline.py, not canonical state.
# latest_brief.json and latest.html are re-built each morning from baseline + caches.
# Dated subdirs (e.g. system/published/daily/2026-05-24/) are ephemeral run outputs.
# To archive a specific brief, copy it intentionally and commit with a clear message.
system/published/

# Auto-snapshots from mutations.py — git history already preserves prior state.
# Date-tagged milestone snapshots (e.g. baseline_index.2026-05-12.json) ARE versioned.
system/_snapshots/*.pre-*.json
system/_snapshots/*.pre-*.jsonl
system/_snapshots/*.pre-*.md
system/_snapshots/*.pre-*.yaml
# HTML pre-publish snapshots (RB 9.9: added to cover publish.py html snapshots).
system/_snapshots/*.pre-*.html

# Weekly file-copy backup from friday_eow_routine.py (RB-2026-08-24) — same
# rationale as system/_snapshots/ above: git history already preserves prior
# state, and this copies multi-megabyte files (baseline_index.json,
# ecosystem_intelligence.json) every week, which would bloat the repo
# indefinitely if tracked. The backup's value is a local, git-independent
# restore point, not something that itself needs version control.
system/_backups/

# Live inbox data — operator-private calendar and email. Fetched per session.
system/inbox/*.json
system/inbox/conversation_artifacts/**

# Auto-generated daily output — rebuilt each morning from canonical state.
system/today.md

# Generated .xlsx exports from ecosystem_export.py — rebuilt on demand from
# system/ecosystem_intelligence.json, not canonical state.
system/exports/

# Project-root scratch output for ad-hoc .docx/.xlsx exports and QA/
# comparison passes (brief_compare/, canonical_brief_qa/, docx_qa/) --
# same "regeneratable, not canonical state" rationale as system/exports/
# above. Canonical documents live under customers_prospects/accounts/
# <slug>/briefs/current/ and /current/; this is local working output.
/deliverables/

# Persistent memory store — operator-private runtime data.
system/strategic_memory.json

# Tooling directory — local development helpers, not part of the RB product.
.tools/

# Legacy thread exports / transfer bundles. Treat as source artifacts, not canonical state.
RB 8.0 transfer data/**

# Employer policy source documents — contain employer-confidential text.
# Only the extracted structured YAML under system/employers/*/policies/ is committed.
system/employers/*/source_docs/**

# Microsoft Office lock files (created while a .docx/.xlsx/.pptx is open).
~$*

# Claude Code local-machine config — permissions/paths specific to this machine,
# and active git worktree checkouts. Not shared state.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Ad-hoc scratch workspaces for deck/document generation (contain node_modules,
# rendered previews, intermediate build dirs) — regeneratable, not RB system state.
# RB-2026-09-05: bare .tmp/ was missing from this pattern (only .tmp_*/ globs
# matched) and had accidentally committed a node_modules tree under
# .tmp/pollo-title/ -- untracked via `git rm -r --cached` before adding this.
.tmp/
.tmp_*/
.codex_work/
# RB-2026-09-19: same pattern as .tmp/ above -- document-rendering fidelity
# checks (a_render/b_render/diff_pages triplets against reference briefs),
# confirmed via inspection to be verification scratch, not final deliverables
# (real Background Briefs live under customers_prospects/.../briefs/current/).
# Untracked when found; not deleted here -- see the working-tree cleanup note
# in RBB_TOKEN_EFFICIENT_ARCHITECTURE_SCOPE_2026-09-19.md before removing it.
.codex-tmp/

# ChatGPT Intelligence Drop (RB-2026-09-19) — the README and the packet
# contract template are real, committed specification; the packets
# themselves (deep-research evidence .md/.png dropped for the next sweep)
# are local runtime intelligence, already captured into system/captures/ by
# the time the sweep runs, same reasoning as the live inbox rule above.
system/inbox/chatgpt_intelligence_drop/*
!system/inbox/chatgpt_intelligence_drop/README

# Adaptive research scheduler runtime telemetry — operational churn, not
# durable state. (deep_research_coverage.json in the same directory is
# durable scheduler state and stays tracked.)
system/research/adaptive_research_usage.jsonl

# Node.js dependency trees -- same recurring problem as the .tmp/pollo-title/
# node_modules incident noted above. The project-root one is actually a
# symlink to a Codex runtime cache outside the repo (~/.cache/codex-runtimes/
# .../node_modules), not a real local install -- no trailing slash, so the
# pattern matches the symlink itself, not just a real directory named this.
node_modules

# Runtime file locks (e.g. competitor_intelligence_common.py's
# _registry_lock() -- RB-DEFECT-071 atomic-write fix). Concurrency-control
# artifacts, not persistent state; a stale committed lock on a fresh clone
# would look like a lock already held. Caught after accidentally committing
# one during 2026-09-19 working-tree cleanup.
*.lock

# Weekly-plan-carryover consumption snapshots — same rationale as the other
# _snapshots/*.pre-*.* patterns above (git history isn't the restore point
# for these; weekly_plan_generator.py's own consume-and-unlink step is the
# real lifecycle, confirmed already running normally as of 2026-09-19).
system/_snapshots/weekly_plan_carryover.consumed-*.json

# LibreOffice lock files (created while a spreadsheet/doc is open)
.~lock.*#
system/artifacts/jeff_coffland_product_map/genius_n_review/source.pptx
